  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH and Food Security Response in Deir EzZor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 - the action focuses on improving WASH through various interventions aligned with DG ECHO priorities and the HRP 2023. This includes repairing water networks, promoting hygiene behaviour, and rehabilitating WASH facilities in schools.  2 - Oxfam will provide MPCA to vulnerable households (HHs) in six instalments to cover basic needs. This assistance is expected to improve food consumption and reduce negative coping strategies. This result will also contribute to strengthening the Cash Working Group (CWG) in Syria by supporting the CWG co -chair position.  3 - Oxfam will rehabilitate one bakery to increase the availability and access to subsidized bread, addressing food insecurity. This intervention aligns with the objective of improving communities&apos; resilience and livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
